{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069/events","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069","id":824498131,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU4MjQ0OTgxMzE=","number":70069,"title":"[ML] effective_max_model_memory_limit may be too low in autoscaling environment","user":{"login":"droberts195","id":7405510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MDU1MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7405510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195","html_url":"https://github.com/droberts195","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":23173,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE3Mw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/%3Ebug","name":">bug","color":"b60205","default":false,"description":null},{"id":912833043,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5MTI4MzMwNDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/:ml","name":":ml","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Machine learning"},{"id":1977209897,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTc3MjA5ODk3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/Team:ML","name":"Team:ML","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Meta label for the ML team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2021-03-08T12:08:00Z","updated_at":"2021-03-17T10:36:24Z","closed_at":"2021-03-17T10:36:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"One of the outputs from the `_ml/info` API is `effective_max_model_memory_limit`.  This value is intended to be a hint for the UI about the highest sensible `model_memory_limit` to suggest taking into account both hard limits configured in `xpack.ml.max_model_memory_limit` and the size of available ML nodes, the idea being to stop users from creating jobs that can never be opened in the cluster.\r\n\r\nThe logic used to calculate `effective_max_model_memory_limit` does not take into account the value of the recently added `xpack.ml.max_ml_node_size` setting.  This leads to two possible problems:\r\n\r\n1. In a cluster with no ML nodes currently but autoscaling enabled we do not consider all available information so do not return a value for `effective_max_model_memory_limit` when we could.\r\n2. In a cluster with small ML nodes and autoscaling enabled we base `effective_max_model_memory_limit` on the size of these small nodes rather than the size that autoscaling could scale those nodes up to if necessary.\r\n\r\nProblem 2 is likely to manifest in the case where a user has some small ML jobs, then decides to create one that would ideally have a large `model_memory_limit`.  The UI will guide them to set a `model_memory_limit` that is suboptimally small on the assumption that new ML nodes added to the cluster will be the same size as the current ones.","closed_by":{"login":"droberts195","id":7405510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MDU1MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7405510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195","html_url":"https://github.com/droberts195","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droberts195/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/70069/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}